```

That got messy. Simpler approach: the game's frame loop is `frame(now)` inside closure. I can measure the interval between rAF callbacks with a co-registered rAF loop on the same page:

```js
let prev = 0; const deltas = [];
function probe(t){ if(prev) deltas.push(t-prev); prev=t; requestAnimationFrame(probe); }
```
Deltas show frame pacing but not JS time. To get JS time of game's callback, I can monkeypatch requestAnimationFrame BEFORE the game's next registration: the game re-registers `frame` every frame via requestAnimationFrame(frame). If I wrap rAF so every registered callback gets timed, the wrapper persists because the game calls window.requestAnimationFrame each frame.

